---
/**
 * How privacy works, in plain words. /privacy (the policy) and /security
 * stay the documents of record; this page explains and links to them.
 */
import Detail from '../layouts/Detail.astro';
import DetailSection from '../components/DetailSection.astro';
import PrivacyFlow from '../components/detail/PrivacyFlow.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
---

<Detail
  title="How privacy works"
  heading="How privacy works"
  lead="Your transactions and budget are encrypted on your iPhone before they sync. Our server stores them but can’t read them."
  path="/how-privacy-works"
>
  <PrivacyFlow />

  <DetailSection id="new-phone" title="A new or lost phone">
    <p>
      On a new iPhone, you unlock your data with your passkey, which syncs in iCloud Keychain, or with your 12‑word recovery phrase. A password signs you in but
      doesn’t unlock your data.
    </p>
    <p>Keep the 12 words somewhere safe. We can’t reset them for you, because we don’t hold the key to your data.</p>
  </DetailSection>

  <DetailSection id="no-bank-login" title="No bank login, no ads" tint>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>No bank login.</strong> Hasala reads the alert emails your bank already sends. It never asks for your banking password or card number, and it
        can’t move money.
      </li>
      <li><strong>No ads or tracking in the app.</strong> The app contains no analytics or tracking tools.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>This website counts visits in totals only.</strong> It uses Cloudflare Web Analytics, which sets no cookies and isn’t linked to you or your Hasala
        account. Invite, waitlist and account‑freeze links aren’t counted.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Google API Limited Use.</strong> Hasala follows Google’s API Services User Data Policy, including the Limited Use requirements. What it reads from
        Gmail is used only to find your bank transactions and show them to you.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </DetailSection>

  <DetailSection id="documents" title="The full details">
    <p>
      The <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> lists what we collect, why, and how long we keep it. <a href="/security">Security</a> explains how Hasala protects your data and
      how to report a problem. Questions: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.privacyEmail}`}>{SITE.privacyEmail}</a>.
    </p>
  </DetailSection>
</Detail>
